From ac05e7f49063a5bf1292fb6b5e5e76a729e287e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: the item menu's Create shortcut works, and Pin to
 Start

The item menu of a file or folder (MENU_SHV_FILE: File Explorer's right-click, and the desktop's on the Menu key or
Shift+F10) offered "Create Link", and the command did nothing: its id had no handler ("Unhandled verb" in the log). The
owner met that item and found no shortcut anywhere (2026-11-06).

- dlls/shell32/shell32.rc, po/*.po: the item reads "Create &shortcut" (the msgid changes in all 49 translation files so
  their translations are kept; English's own msgstr in en.po and en_US.po said "Create &Link" and now says it too; French
  now "raccourci"), and "Pi&n to Start" follows it, translated for the ten guided-setup languages, each with an access
  key of its own (the two items' keys differ in every one, so one key press runs the command).
- dlls/shell32/shlview_cmenu.c: the id and the verbs "link" and "pintostartscreen" make, for each selected item that is a
  file or folder, a "<name> - Shortcut.lnk" on the user's Desktop, or in Start's Programs and pinned, through
  wine/ps5/pw_shell_shortcut.h (the code File Explorer's More menu runs; names and pin list host-tested in
  src/pw_shortcut.h). An item with no file path (This PC, the Recycle Bin) is skipped.
- dlls/shell32/shresdef.h: FCIDM_SHVIEW_PINSTART.
